; Entity handler: patroller moving down (kind 4)
;
; The handler of the enemies that move along a vertical line: green and yellow spiders (rooms 3, 14, 16, 19), the
; green flies of room 12 and the red fireballs of rooms 22 and 23. Which one it is depends on the sprite description
; of its room record. A record of kind 4 starts moving down (this handler), a record of kind 5 starts moving up
; (#R$B283); the two handlers turn the slot into each other at the ends of the patrol (stack scheme and slot fields
; as in #R$B2A6, #R$B2D4).
; .
; The y coordinate goes down by the speed each frame; when its high byte reaches the lower turning point (+5) the
; handler word of the slot is rewritten with #R$B283. The sprite is placed at (x, y) through #R$B380 (x is a multiple
; of 4, so the shift phase is 0), which tests the hit box and draws the second frame table.
; .
; Slot fields used: +2 word speed (8.8, 2-pixel units per frame), +4 byte upper turning point of y, +5 byte lower
; turning point, +6 word x (high byte only), +8 word y (8.8).
; .
; Hardware: none.
;
; SP Slot address + 2
@label=UpdateWalkDown
c$B344 POP BC        ; speed
 $B345 POP DE        ; D lower turning point, E upper
 $B346 POP HL        ; x (8.8); only its high byte is used
 $B347 LD A,H        ; A = x in 2-pixel units
 $B348 EX AF,AF'     ; kept in A'
 $B349 POP HL        ; y (8.8)
 $B34A ADD HL,BC     ; y goes down
 $B34B PUSH HL       ;
 $B34C POP HL        ; SP is back at slot+10
 $B34D LD A,H        ; y in 2-pixel units
 $B34E CP D          ; reached the lower turning point?
 $B34F JR C,$B35F    ; no: go on
 $B351 LD HL,$FFF8   ; -8: back to slot+2
 $B354 ADD HL,SP     ;
 $B355 LD SP,HL      ;
 $B356 LD HL,$B283   ; from the next frame the creature goes up
 $B359 PUSH HL       ; written over the handler word at slot+0
 $B35A POP HL        ; pop the handler again
 $B35B POP BC        ; pop speed, limits, x and y again
 $B35C POP DE        ;
 $B35D POP HL        ;
 $B35E POP HL        ;
*$B35F EX AF,AF'     ; A = x
 $B360 LD D,A        ; D = x
 $B361 POP BC        ; skip the unused word at +10
 $B362 LD E,H        ; E = y
 $B363 JR $B380      ; place the sprite, test the hit box, draw (facing down)
